From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: RequestCommitAsync completes at the next frame; ICompositionGraphicsDevice2

ICompositor5::RequestCommitAsync gave an action already completed, and
put_Completed ran the handler there and then. Avalonia 11's render loop
(WinUiCompositorConnection, the "DwmRenderTimerLoop" thread) asks for the
next commit from inside that handler and sets the same handler on it, so it
recursed until the thread's stack overflowed: ShareX 22.4 and ImageGlass 10
died at start. On Windows the action is Started until the commit has been
shown and its handler runs then, on the compositor's thread. Now the actions
wait on their compositor; a frame timer (16 ms) on the compositor's notify
window completes them and runs their handlers from its message loop. A
handler set on a finished action still runs at once; a compositor that ends
cancels its waiting actions.

Avalonia then draws its windows into a surface from ICompositionGraphicsDevice2
CreateDrawingSurface2 (sized in pixels, starting at 0x0, Resized through
ICompositionDrawingSurfaceInterop). The graphics device now has that
interface (CreateVirtualDrawingSurface is still E_NOTIMPL), and a surface's
Size is what was asked, 0x0 included (its bitmap stays at least 1x1). Without
it Avalonia made a new graphics device every frame and its windows were black.

Gates: test/compcommitasync-gate.sh, test/compdevice2-gate.sh (compweak's
expectation is now an action Started until the next frame); mutants
SG_MUTANT_COMMIT_ACTION_DONE_AT_ONCE, SG_MUTANT_NO_GRAPHICS_DEVICE2.
